<title>UK: NWE straight-run fuel oil flat but supply healthy.</title>
<headline>NWE straight-run fuel oil flat but supply healthy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil prices were notionally unchanged on Tuesday but dealers said liquidity had been sucked out of the market by an absence of traders.</p>
<p>One refiner said he thought fob prices for North Sea cargoes were around $140 a tonne. &quot;There are a few cargoes around but we will not see how much demand there is until business starts again next year.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
